WEBVTT

1
00:00:54,154 --> 00:00:59,727
(♪♪♪)

2
00:01:00,962 --> 00:01:02,630
OFFICER 1:
Blacklance, step up.

3
00:01:02,664 --> 00:01:04,832
(♪♪♪)

4
00:01:14,474 --> 00:01:16,844
OFFICER 2:
All right, Richie,
you're good to go.

5
00:01:16,878 --> 00:01:19,413
(♪♪♪)

6
00:01:37,497 --> 00:01:39,834
LEON:
Hey, over here.
I think they're over here.

7
00:01:42,537 --> 00:01:44,772
LEON:
Go, go, go.
Up on the cliff.

8
00:01:44,806 --> 00:01:49,109
(♪♪♪)

9
00:01:59,286 --> 00:02:00,722
LEON:
Al, why'd you stop?

10
00:02:03,457 --> 00:02:05,960
Oh, shit.

11
00:02:05,994 --> 00:02:10,197
(♪♪♪)

12
00:02:22,877 --> 00:02:26,313
(♪♪♪)

13
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:42,830
TEDDY:
Yeah, I saw then
that it was Bradley.

14
00:02:42,864 --> 00:02:44,197
Albert's brother.

15
00:02:44,231 --> 00:02:47,001
I know the family,
so I'll make the notification.

16
00:02:47,035 --> 00:02:48,301
Okay.

17
00:02:49,971 --> 00:02:52,774
(POLICE RADIO CHATTER)

18
00:02:54,142 --> 00:02:57,277
COMMENTATOR (ON RADIO):
(INDISTINCT SPEECH)

19
00:02:57,310 --> 00:02:59,080
<i>Hold the ball.</i>

20
00:02:59,113 --> 00:03:01,649
<i>Look at your stride</i>
<i>once in a while,</i>

21
00:03:01,683 --> 00:03:04,752
<i>just to offset the timing</i>
<i>and tempo of the baseline.</i>

22
00:03:10,091 --> 00:03:11,358
Hey, Dad.

23
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:12,660
Hey.

24
00:03:21,602 --> 00:03:22,870
(CHUCKLES)

25
00:03:22,904 --> 00:03:24,404
Stop.

26
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:31,946
Practice tomorrow?

27
00:03:31,979 --> 00:03:33,480
Yeah, 6:30.

28
00:03:34,816 --> 00:03:36,050
TEDDY:
Need a ride?

29
00:03:36,084 --> 00:03:37,350
Nah, it's all good.

30
00:03:37,384 --> 00:03:39,554
Coach is gonna swing by
and give me a lift there.

31
00:03:42,657 --> 00:03:45,225
TEDDY:
Albert found him in the woods
behind the clubhouse.

32
00:03:45,258 --> 00:03:46,961
DYANI:
I just can't believe it.

33
00:03:46,994 --> 00:03:49,764
His mother and now his brother?

34
00:03:49,797 --> 00:03:51,498
(SIGHS)

35
00:03:52,667 --> 00:03:53,835
You okay?

36
00:03:55,703 --> 00:03:58,539
Yeah, it's just...

37
00:03:58,573 --> 00:03:59,974
I know.

38
00:04:02,844 --> 00:04:04,545
I'm here.

39
00:04:07,915 --> 00:04:09,717
(KISSES)

40
00:04:10,818 --> 00:04:13,721
DYANI (VO):
<i>You're a good man, Teddy.</i>

41
00:04:13,755 --> 00:04:16,824
TEDDY (VO):
<i>I just look at Albert</i>
<i>and I see our boy.</i>

42
00:04:19,026 --> 00:04:20,862
<i>I see all those kids.</i>

43
00:04:24,132 --> 00:04:27,467
(♪♪♪)

44
00:04:34,709 --> 00:04:38,679
(♪♪♪)

45
00:04:50,792 --> 00:04:52,760
(EXHALES SMOKE)

46
00:05:02,804 --> 00:05:04,605
What the...

47
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,223
I got ya. Hurry!

48
00:05:22,256 --> 00:05:25,526
(♪♪♪)

49
00:05:34,135 --> 00:05:35,335
There he is.

50
00:05:35,368 --> 00:05:37,572
(INDISCERNIBLE SPEECH)

51
00:05:37,605 --> 00:05:39,106
And boom. You wanna make
that elbow

52
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:40,908
about 90 degrees with your eye.

53
00:05:40,942 --> 00:05:44,045
(♪♪♪)

54
00:05:56,423 --> 00:05:58,259
STERLING:
You really clean?

55
00:05:58,292 --> 00:06:01,394
RICHIE:
Cigarettes. That's it.

56
00:06:01,428 --> 00:06:03,130
Hardest to kick.

57
00:06:03,164 --> 00:06:05,132
STERLING:
State Pen did you good.

58
00:06:07,802 --> 00:06:10,071
Not the pen.

59
00:06:10,104 --> 00:06:12,773
Place makes you wanna be
swinging from the ceiling.

60
00:06:15,309 --> 00:06:17,410
It was the brothers
I was with.

61
00:06:18,411 --> 00:06:22,149
OG natives.
Real men.

62
00:06:22,183 --> 00:06:24,185
STERLING:
That's what I needed, bro.

63
00:06:24,218 --> 00:06:26,087
Mentors and shit.

64
00:06:27,454 --> 00:06:29,456
Ain't nothing
but kids out here, bro.

65
00:06:30,858 --> 00:06:35,796
Guys like us, we're like,
OGs in these streets now.

66
00:06:35,830 --> 00:06:37,397
Isn't that crazy?

67
00:06:37,430 --> 00:06:39,233
(MOANING)

68
00:06:39,267 --> 00:06:40,835
(PUFFS SMOKES)

69
00:06:40,868 --> 00:06:43,771
Yeah, I can't quit.
Not before I do work.

70
00:06:43,804 --> 00:06:46,741
(MOANING)

71
00:06:57,118 --> 00:06:59,486
Yo, I'm home.

72
00:07:02,023 --> 00:07:04,158
(EXHALES)

73
00:07:04,992 --> 00:07:06,560
What's up, Winchell?

74
00:07:07,494 --> 00:07:10,231
Richie.
When'd you get out?

75
00:07:10,264 --> 00:07:12,867
Yesterday.

76
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:15,435
Thought we'd throw
a welcome home party.

77
00:07:15,468 --> 00:07:20,641
(♪♪♪)

78
00:07:28,416 --> 00:07:30,751
Still in your old line
of work, huh?

79
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,155
Gotta pay rent somehow.

80
00:07:35,756 --> 00:07:41,028
Heard you're repping D.E.P.
Finally picked a side.

81
00:07:41,062 --> 00:07:42,897
The wrong side.

82
00:07:44,198 --> 00:07:46,400
You know how it is, man.

83
00:07:46,434 --> 00:07:48,436
Can't last as an independent
in this game.

84
00:07:48,468 --> 00:07:51,939
(♪♪♪)

85
00:08:00,381 --> 00:08:03,451
How does
a two-bit tweaker dealer

86
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:06,520
get the blessing of Luke
Spencer to join the Posse?

87
00:08:08,289 --> 00:08:10,591
Just comes down to money.

88
00:08:11,525 --> 00:08:14,061
RICHIE:
Yeah. It always does.

89
00:08:15,596 --> 00:08:19,033
How much did Luke pay you
to sell me tainted dope?

90
00:08:19,066 --> 00:08:20,101
WINCHELL:
Richie.

91
00:08:20,134 --> 00:08:22,837
No, don't. Not to him.

92
00:08:24,171 --> 00:08:26,841
RICHIE:
You know,

93
00:08:26,874 --> 00:08:30,745
I don't blame anyone
for wanting me dead.

94
00:08:33,547 --> 00:08:38,619
That's just the price of
being a player in the game.

95
00:08:42,990 --> 00:08:44,558
But my sister?

96
00:08:45,993 --> 00:08:49,563
Look, I was threatened
if I didn't--

97
00:08:49,597 --> 00:08:51,232
How'd I know your sister
was gonna be the one

98
00:08:51,265 --> 00:08:52,500
to take your dope and go--

99
00:08:52,533 --> 00:08:54,503
(GROANS)

100
00:08:54,535 --> 00:08:56,604
(CHOKES)

101
00:08:56,637 --> 00:08:58,606
What are you doing?
What are you doing?

102
00:08:58,639 --> 00:09:03,611
No, no! No! No! No!

103
00:09:04,612 --> 00:09:06,781
(GRUNTING)

104
00:09:15,423 --> 00:09:18,059
(SCREAMS)

105
00:09:24,965 --> 00:09:26,233
RICHIE:
You know what's crazy?

106
00:09:26,267 --> 00:09:28,269
You and I used to kick it
and play video games

107
00:09:28,302 --> 00:09:30,204
all the time as kids.

108
00:09:30,237 --> 00:09:31,705
(GROANS)

109
00:09:31,739 --> 00:09:33,274
Sleepovers and shit.

110
00:09:33,307 --> 00:09:36,043
(WINCHELL GROANS)

111
00:09:37,278 --> 00:09:38,379
Please, Richie.

112
00:09:38,412 --> 00:09:41,182
(WINCHELL CHOKES)

113
00:09:48,856 --> 00:09:50,691
Let's get the fuck outta here.

114
00:09:58,999 --> 00:10:00,535
-Shit.
-Shit.

115
00:10:00,569 --> 00:10:02,937
-Oh, shit.
-Chill, man. I got this.

116
00:10:07,475 --> 00:10:09,477
Hey, officer.
They went that way.

117
00:10:09,511 --> 00:10:10,978
Hey, take a step back
from the vehicle.

118
00:10:11,011 --> 00:10:12,246
Chill, man.
We're the ones that called you.

119
00:10:12,279 --> 00:10:14,148
Step back from the vehicle.
Show me your hands.

120
00:10:14,181 --> 00:10:15,916
Hands out of your po--

121
00:10:17,051 --> 00:10:20,054
(SCREAMING)

122
00:10:20,087 --> 00:10:25,693
(♪♪♪)

123
00:10:35,102 --> 00:10:38,405
(♪♪♪)

124
00:10:50,117 --> 00:10:54,221
(♪♪♪)

125
00:11:10,304 --> 00:11:13,274
(SIGHS, GRUNTS)

126
00:11:25,419 --> 00:11:28,289
(INDISCERNIBLE CHATTER)

127
00:11:33,027 --> 00:11:34,828
NEWSREADER (ON RADIO):
<i>Three people are dead,</i>
<i>including</i>

128
00:11:34,862 --> 00:11:36,997
<i>a rookie police officer,</i>
<i>at a grisly scene</i>

129
00:11:37,031 --> 00:11:38,866
<i>in the city's north side.</i>

130
00:11:38,899 --> 00:11:40,868
<i>At a press conference</i>
<i>earlier this morning,</i>

131
00:11:40,901 --> 00:11:43,103
<i>Chief Jerry Garland confirmed</i>
<i>that the department</i>

132
00:11:43,137 --> 00:11:45,206
<i>is on the hunt</i>
<i>for two unknown suspects,</i>

133
00:11:45,239 --> 00:11:46,807
<i>who are believed</i>
<i>to be connected</i>

134
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:48,075
<i>to native street gangs</i>
<i>from the troubled</i>

135
00:11:48,108 --> 00:11:49,644
<i>Thunderstone Reservation.</i>

136
00:11:49,678 --> 00:11:51,145
<i>Tribal Police</i>
<i>and Reliance County</i>

137
00:11:51,178 --> 00:11:52,746
<i>Sheriff's Department</i>
<i>have both pledged</i>

138
00:11:52,780 --> 00:11:54,815
<i>their full cooperation,</i>
<i>despite last month's</i>

139
00:11:54,848 --> 00:11:56,817
<i>very public dispute</i>
<i>over criminal jurisdiction</i>

140
00:11:56,850 --> 00:11:58,052
<i>of tribal land.</i>

141
00:11:58,085 --> 00:11:59,887
<i>Police have stressed</i>
<i>that the two suspects</i>

142
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:02,389
<i>are believed to be</i>
<i>armed and dangerous.</i>

143
00:12:02,423 --> 00:12:05,492
<i>♪ Three, two, one ♪</i>

144
00:12:05,527 --> 00:12:07,428
<i>♪ When we were young ♪</i>

145
00:12:07,461 --> 00:12:09,496
<i>♪ There were so many</i>
<i>new things ♪</i>

146
00:12:09,531 --> 00:12:12,701
<i>♪ For us to find ♪</i>

147
00:12:12,733 --> 00:12:17,338
<i>♪ And time was never</i>
<i>on our mind ♪</i>

148
00:12:23,777 --> 00:12:25,614
So, no barrier from the perps?

149
00:12:25,647 --> 00:12:29,783
Nah, I took that shit out.
Put the regular seats back in.

150
00:12:33,555 --> 00:12:35,389
Where you from?

151
00:12:35,422 --> 00:12:36,824
Tulsa, Oklahoma.

152
00:12:36,857 --> 00:12:39,193
Yeah, I know that.
I mean your people.

153
00:12:40,828 --> 00:12:42,530
I'm American.

154
00:12:42,564 --> 00:12:44,064
Oh.

155
00:12:44,098 --> 00:12:46,701
What is it, Scala?
What is that, Italian?

156
00:12:46,735 --> 00:12:49,303
You, uh, celebrate Columbus Day
and all that?

157
00:12:50,605 --> 00:12:52,172
I'm Greek.

158
00:12:54,208 --> 00:12:56,944
Well, we're all just
squatters here, Toto.

159
00:12:56,977 --> 00:12:58,045
Wait, you're not...

160
00:12:58,078 --> 00:13:01,081
Nope.
Grew up over the line.

161
00:13:01,115 --> 00:13:04,552
They used to bus some kids
into my school from the res,

162
00:13:04,586 --> 00:13:06,320
and I was too poor
and too brown

163
00:13:06,353 --> 00:13:07,821
for the white kids,
so they lumped me in

164
00:13:07,855 --> 00:13:09,624
with the natives.

165
00:13:09,658 --> 00:13:10,824
And then I married me one.

166
00:13:10,858 --> 00:13:12,126
(CHUCKLES)

167
00:13:12,159 --> 00:13:13,427
Ah.

168
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:15,129
It was the '80s.
Shit was crazy.

169
00:13:15,162 --> 00:13:17,064
(LAUGHS)

170
00:13:19,066 --> 00:13:21,168
Got any Indians out there
in Tulsa?

171
00:13:22,637 --> 00:13:24,271
Uh, the indigenous people
there are--

172
00:13:24,305 --> 00:13:25,839
Indians.

173
00:13:26,974 --> 00:13:28,208
I don't think we're supposed
to say--

174
00:13:28,242 --> 00:13:30,477
Oh, don't do that, rookie.
You might hurt yourself.

175
00:13:32,846 --> 00:13:34,114
I've got four years on.

176
00:13:34,148 --> 00:13:35,349
In a bigger department
than this, so--

177
00:13:35,382 --> 00:13:38,218
Bigger ain't shit.
This is tribal land.

178
00:13:38,252 --> 00:13:40,487
And lose that PC bullshit
they drilled into your brain

179
00:13:40,522 --> 00:13:41,422
in the big city.

180
00:13:41,455 --> 00:13:43,891
That shit don't jive out here,
all right?

181
00:13:43,924 --> 00:13:45,459
Indigenous.

182
00:13:45,492 --> 00:13:49,163
Is that what they are now?
According to who? You?

183
00:13:49,196 --> 00:13:51,932
Hmm?
Your white college professor?

184
00:13:51,965 --> 00:13:54,468
Some pretendian who's never
even been to the res?

185
00:13:54,502 --> 00:13:56,904
Listen, you take
that colonizer guilt bullshit

186
00:13:56,937 --> 00:14:00,374
and you bury it somewhere
deep because I'll tell you,

187
00:14:00,407 --> 00:14:02,276
when you're in a foot chase
down here,

188
00:14:02,309 --> 00:14:04,211
you're gonna be yelling out
her description like,

189
00:14:04,244 --> 00:14:05,979
(MIMICS PANTING)

190
00:14:06,013 --> 00:14:09,517
"Indian male,
running northbound fast!

191
00:14:09,551 --> 00:14:13,887
He's, uh, approximately 5'10",
130 pounds, red skin, feather,

192
00:14:13,921 --> 00:14:15,523
armed with a tomahawk!"

193
00:14:15,557 --> 00:14:17,358
(LAUGHS)

194
00:14:21,596 --> 00:14:25,299
Oh, shit. Relax, Toto.

195
00:14:26,867 --> 00:14:30,070
Oh, these are tough people
out here.

196
00:14:30,104 --> 00:14:32,072
No one's gonna get offended
by some here today,

197
00:14:32,106 --> 00:14:34,308
gone tomorrow
Greek rookie res cop.

198
00:14:34,341 --> 00:14:36,544
DISPATCHER (ON RADIO):
<i>Bravo 5-5, Bravo 5-5.</i>

199
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:39,748
You waiting
for smoke signals?

200
00:14:39,781 --> 00:14:40,981
Oh.

201
00:14:43,484 --> 00:14:44,952
Go for Bravo 5-5.

202
00:14:44,985 --> 00:14:47,856
DISPATCHER (ON RADIO):
<i>Bravo 5-5, neighbors advising</i>
<i>of trespassers</i>

203
00:14:47,888 --> 00:14:49,356
<i>inside a vacant house.</i>

204
00:14:49,390 --> 00:14:51,793
<i>It's the, uh,</i>
<i>doublewide Marty Powers</i>

205
00:14:51,826 --> 00:14:53,026
<i>got stabbed in</i>
<i>back in October.</i>

206
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:55,062
-Can we get an address?
-I know where it's at.

207
00:14:55,095 --> 00:14:59,466
<i>♪ Until our time slips away ♪</i>

208
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:04,204
<i>♪ Slips away ♪</i>

209
00:15:14,081 --> 00:15:15,550
TEDDY:
Relax.

210
00:15:15,583 --> 00:15:18,152
I'll go first and I don't need
a bullet in my back.

211
00:15:36,871 --> 00:15:38,372
A lot of these vacant homes
don't even have

212
00:15:38,405 --> 00:15:40,007
addresses anymore.

213
00:15:40,875 --> 00:15:42,443
So what do I do
if I need backup

214
00:15:42,476 --> 00:15:45,479
and I don't know
where Marty Power got stabbed?

215
00:15:45,513 --> 00:15:46,748
I don't know.

216
00:15:46,781 --> 00:15:48,148
Fifth house on the left,
look for my car,

217
00:15:48,182 --> 00:15:50,451
the lights are on.
You'll figure it out.

218
00:15:52,887 --> 00:15:55,523
Feds built some homes
closer to town.

219
00:15:58,425 --> 00:16:01,028
That's where old Marty Powers
is now.

220
00:16:04,164 --> 00:16:06,400
They promised
clean running water.

221
00:16:07,267 --> 00:16:09,136
They're taking
their time though.

222
00:16:10,204 --> 00:16:12,640
Meanwhile, every passing hobo
and meth head

223
00:16:12,674 --> 00:16:15,242
finds these empty places
to hang loose for a while.

224
00:16:18,913 --> 00:16:21,114
Who's in there?

225
00:16:22,382 --> 00:16:23,952
Don't surprise me,
motherfucker,

226
00:16:23,984 --> 00:16:25,252
or you'll get shot!

227
00:16:26,987 --> 00:16:28,088
Go after him.

228
00:16:28,121 --> 00:16:30,090
SAMMY:
Go, hurry, hurry, come on.

229
00:16:30,758 --> 00:16:32,359
Go, go, go, go, go!

230
00:16:32,392 --> 00:16:34,963
TEDDY:
Hold it!
Let me see those hands.

231
00:16:34,995 --> 00:16:37,297
Turn around.
Let me see you.

232
00:16:40,434 --> 00:16:42,302
(LAUGHS)

233
00:16:42,336 --> 00:16:45,239
Look at these
two criminal masterminds.

234
00:16:48,275 --> 00:16:50,277
Jordy P is his nickname.

235
00:16:53,581 --> 00:16:55,517
VM for Vice Mob.

236
00:16:55,550 --> 00:16:58,620
Sometimes they brand out here
along with the gang ink.

237
00:16:58,653 --> 00:17:02,022
22 for V, 13 for M.

238
00:17:02,557 --> 00:17:04,626
(LAUGHS)

239
00:17:04,659 --> 00:17:08,095
Jordy, you are literally
a walking mugshot.

240
00:17:10,565 --> 00:17:11,799
Watch him.

241
00:17:13,267 --> 00:17:17,972
See a lot of D.E.P. out here.
Dead End Posse.

242
00:17:18,006 --> 00:17:19,607
Hmm. Clever.

243
00:17:28,482 --> 00:17:31,418
Mace. Nice catch.

244
00:17:32,119 --> 00:17:34,254
Next customer.

245
00:17:34,288 --> 00:17:36,123
Going into your pockets,
anything gonna stick me?

246
00:17:36,156 --> 00:17:37,525
I don't think so.

247
00:17:37,559 --> 00:17:39,159
Mm-hmm.

248
00:17:42,797 --> 00:17:45,098
This doesn't qualify?

249
00:17:50,905 --> 00:17:55,375
This is why I love my job.
You know what I just did?

250
00:17:55,409 --> 00:17:57,311
Hey, keep your hands out
of your pockets, please.

251
00:17:59,346 --> 00:18:02,984
I just prevented the robbing
of a gas station,

252
00:18:03,017 --> 00:18:04,619
the stabbing
of some I.B.N. loser,

253
00:18:04,652 --> 00:18:06,486
or potentially one of these
two numpties getting shot

254
00:18:06,521 --> 00:18:09,456
by the police.
I am a goddamn hero.

255
00:18:09,489 --> 00:18:11,059
SANDRA:
All right, let me get some IDs.

256
00:18:11,091 --> 00:18:13,360
No, no, no.
We're not doing that.

257
00:18:20,835 --> 00:18:22,604
You go immediately home.

258
00:18:22,637 --> 00:18:24,505
If I find either one of you
back out here

259
00:18:24,539 --> 00:18:26,941
or anywhere else
other than home today,

260
00:18:26,975 --> 00:18:28,241
I promise you,
you will be remanded.

261
00:18:28,275 --> 00:18:30,612
I will make sure that happens
one way or another.

262
00:18:32,580 --> 00:18:33,715
Beat it.

263
00:18:45,325 --> 00:18:47,361
Sorry, weren't we supposed
to run them for, like,

264
00:18:47,394 --> 00:18:49,396
wants and warrants, conditions?

265
00:18:49,429 --> 00:18:50,898
I mean, they're gang members.
Isn't that, like--

266
00:18:50,932 --> 00:18:52,499
Yeah, sure.

267
00:18:52,533 --> 00:18:54,836
Sammy could go in
on a weapons violation.

268
00:18:54,869 --> 00:18:56,738
But tomorrow, his mom is headed
to the city for work

269
00:18:56,771 --> 00:18:58,606
and Sammy watches
her five-year-old twins

270
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:00,074
during the day.

271
00:19:00,108 --> 00:19:01,676
Jordy P. is wanted
in the city for assault.

272
00:19:01,709 --> 00:19:03,645
I mean, they might come
down here and get him.

273
00:19:03,678 --> 00:19:05,546
Or hell, shit, man,
we might just take him up

274
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:06,681
there ourselves.

275
00:19:06,714 --> 00:19:09,249
But I'd rather save that
for a rainy day.

276
00:19:09,851 --> 00:19:11,786
A rainy day?

277
00:19:12,754 --> 00:19:14,022
(LAUGHS)

278
00:19:14,055 --> 00:19:16,490
What was your last
department like?

279
00:19:17,925 --> 00:19:20,128
It was blue collar.
It was a tough beat to work.

280
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:22,229
Yeah, well,
out here it's no collar.

281
00:19:22,262 --> 00:19:24,565
No backup, no resources,
no witnesses.

282
00:19:24,599 --> 00:19:26,934
I mean, hell, sometimes
it's even hard to find a victim.

283
00:19:29,202 --> 00:19:32,974
Res policing is all
about temporary problem solving,

284
00:19:33,007 --> 00:19:35,576
favors and leverage.

285
00:19:35,610 --> 00:19:36,911
You get everyone
in this town through

286
00:19:36,944 --> 00:19:39,446
to the end of the shift
and then you hand the reins

287
00:19:39,479 --> 00:19:41,448
over to the next schmuck.

288
00:19:41,481 --> 00:19:44,251
All right, let's find a dumpster
and process those exhibits.

289
00:19:44,686 --> 00:19:46,486
Teddy.

290
00:19:46,521 --> 00:19:47,755
Uh-huh.

291
00:19:51,358 --> 00:19:54,062
-So you're the new girl?
-Hmm. Sandra.

292
00:19:54,095 --> 00:19:57,364
Darius.
I'm with Reliance County.

293
00:19:57,397 --> 00:19:59,867
Dispatch informed us
about the call.

294
00:19:59,901 --> 00:20:01,135
You guys good?

295
00:20:01,169 --> 00:20:02,637
SANDRA:
Yeah, we're good.

296
00:20:03,871 --> 00:20:05,272
Mm-hmm.

297
00:20:06,239 --> 00:20:08,509
Well, it is a beautiful, crisp,
cool day.

298
00:20:08,543 --> 00:20:11,646
Nothing like some shit rats
to keep us warm and busy, huh?

299
00:20:14,582 --> 00:20:17,552
All right,
call if you need anything.

300
00:20:26,627 --> 00:20:29,530
SANDRA:
Yeah, no, it's--
it's just not what I expected.

301
00:20:29,564 --> 00:20:32,133
My partner is definitely
a character.

302
00:20:32,166 --> 00:20:33,868
(SANDRA CHUCKLES)

303
00:20:35,002 --> 00:20:36,971
No, Mom, don't.

304
00:20:37,004 --> 00:20:38,840
Because I just got here.

305
00:20:38,873 --> 00:20:41,209
You know,
I haven't even settled in yet.

306
00:20:41,241 --> 00:20:42,977
I still need
to get my bearings.

307
00:20:47,215 --> 00:20:51,284
How's Dad doing?
Can I talk to him?

308
00:20:55,890 --> 00:20:58,726
Yeah, no, it's fine.
I-- I know he's busy.

309
00:20:58,760 --> 00:20:59,961
Maybe tomorrow.

310
00:21:01,195 --> 00:21:03,231
Hey, listen, I'm gonna go, uh,
get some sleep.

311
00:21:03,263 --> 00:21:05,365
I'm exhausted.

312
00:21:11,639 --> 00:21:14,709
CEREMONY LEADER:
(SINGS IN NATIVE LANGUAGE)

313
00:21:14,742 --> 00:21:18,880
(♪♪♪)

314
00:21:28,421 --> 00:21:31,993
DUNCAN:
It seems we never stop
mourning, doesn't it?

315
00:21:32,026 --> 00:21:37,031
Chelsea, you've experienced
so much loss over the years,

316
00:21:37,064 --> 00:21:38,733
so much heartache.

317
00:21:38,766 --> 00:21:42,335
It's too much for one person
to bear.

318
00:21:42,369 --> 00:21:45,640
You've raised and guided
our kids in this town.

319
00:21:45,673 --> 00:21:47,842
Even when my own boys
were running amok,

320
00:21:47,875 --> 00:21:49,977
causing me havoc,
they'd come to you

321
00:21:50,011 --> 00:21:52,880
for advice about their troubles.

322
00:21:52,914 --> 00:21:55,716
You were the most
resilient person they knew.

323
00:21:57,317 --> 00:22:00,487
We've always had
to be resilient.

324
00:22:00,521 --> 00:22:05,893
So please believe me
when I say when you hurt,

325
00:22:05,927 --> 00:22:07,962
we all hurt.

326
00:22:07,995 --> 00:22:11,032
When you weep, we all weep.

327
00:22:23,678 --> 00:22:25,012
Chelsea.

328
00:22:26,848 --> 00:22:28,448
CHELSEA:
Luke.

329
00:22:33,754 --> 00:22:35,523
What are you doing here, Luke?

330
00:22:35,556 --> 00:22:38,559
Can't you see
she's going through enough?

331
00:22:38,593 --> 00:22:40,493
You show your face here
of all places--

332
00:22:40,528 --> 00:22:42,797
Don't trip.
I'm not here to cause trouble.

333
00:22:42,830 --> 00:22:46,067
Had no beef with Bradley.
Just paying my respects.

334
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:48,035
You need to leave, Luke.

335
00:22:48,069 --> 00:22:49,704
ANGEL:
Bye.

336
00:22:49,737 --> 00:22:51,873
Rumor is Richie got parole.

337
00:22:51,906 --> 00:22:54,242
Heard stories he's running wild
in the big city.

338
00:22:54,275 --> 00:22:55,375
Heard he might be headed
this way.

339
00:22:55,408 --> 00:22:58,913
-Richie isn't here--
-Richie isn't here.

340
00:22:58,946 --> 00:23:02,449
Richie is not welcome
anywhere near any of us.

341
00:23:03,184 --> 00:23:04,952
I buried a lot of my family,

342
00:23:04,986 --> 00:23:07,855
but he is the only one
who is dead to me.

343
00:23:09,690 --> 00:23:12,392
Then we're good.
Sorry for your loss.

344
00:23:12,425 --> 00:23:14,662
Bradley was a good kid.

345
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:23,971
(♪♪♪)

346
00:23:49,664 --> 00:23:51,165
CHELSEA:
Who's that?

347
00:24:03,443 --> 00:24:05,947
(♪♪♪)

348
00:24:13,921 --> 00:24:15,222
Hey, Mom.

349
00:24:19,961 --> 00:24:21,729
What do you want?

350
00:24:25,132 --> 00:24:30,504
That's all you had to say?
After all these years?

351
00:24:33,441 --> 00:24:35,776
Bradley...

352
00:24:35,810 --> 00:24:39,714
He's been on my mind a lot.

353
00:24:41,282 --> 00:24:44,118
Wish I could see him
one more time.

354
00:24:45,519 --> 00:24:47,955
I know it's gotta be
killing Albert.

355
00:24:47,989 --> 00:24:49,090
How is he?

356
00:24:49,123 --> 00:24:52,626
You leave him alone.
You've done enough.

357
00:24:53,694 --> 00:24:56,230
You really still blame me?

358
00:24:56,263 --> 00:24:59,200
For every problem
this family has?

359
00:24:59,233 --> 00:25:00,868
(SCOFFS)

360
00:25:00,901 --> 00:25:03,871
RICHIE:
Like Leanne didn't show me
how to get high?

361
00:25:04,872 --> 00:25:07,808
Like Leroy didn't show me
how to boost cars?

362
00:25:10,344 --> 00:25:12,013
Just leave.

363
00:25:15,616 --> 00:25:18,753
(TAKES A DRAG AND PUFFS SMOKE)

364
00:25:22,590 --> 00:25:26,761
All these dead
and broken kids, Mom.

365
00:25:29,663 --> 00:25:32,533
What does that say about you?

366
00:25:35,202 --> 00:25:39,807
(♪♪♪)

367
00:25:50,217 --> 00:25:55,556
(♪♪♪)

368
00:26:10,171 --> 00:26:11,939
SANDRA:
A lot of calls come
in through here?

369
00:26:11,972 --> 00:26:13,808
It's the heart
of gang territory.

370
00:26:13,841 --> 00:26:16,877
But only two crews
have any real teeth.

371
00:26:16,911 --> 00:26:20,114
Dead End Posse
and Indian Blood Nation.

372
00:26:25,052 --> 00:26:26,555
Bull.

373
00:26:27,088 --> 00:26:28,589
Teddy.

374
00:26:30,391 --> 00:26:31,892
He's I.B.N.

375
00:26:34,995 --> 00:26:39,834
(♪♪♪)

376
00:26:50,344 --> 00:26:55,883
(♪♪♪)

377
00:26:59,920 --> 00:27:02,423
TRUNK GANGSTER:
What?

378
00:27:02,456 --> 00:27:04,959
You want me to pop this thing
and get you some air?

379
00:27:06,460 --> 00:27:07,695
TRUNK GANGSTER:
Who the fuck is this?

380
00:27:07,728 --> 00:27:10,097
The police. You want out
of this thing or what?

381
00:27:10,131 --> 00:27:13,934
TRUNK GANGSTER:
Ah, shit, man, why are you
harassing me for, dude?

382
00:27:13,968 --> 00:27:18,405
Harassing you?
You're locked in a trunk.

383
00:27:18,439 --> 00:27:21,008
TRUNK GANGSTER:
Is that a crime, officer?
What, you got a warrant?

384
00:27:21,041 --> 00:27:22,810
No one's asking
for your help.

385
00:27:22,843 --> 00:27:24,778
Leave me the fuck alone
to do my time.

386
00:27:25,679 --> 00:27:28,149
All right. Conserve your air.

387
00:27:28,182 --> 00:27:31,986
TRUNK GANGSTER:
Conserve my dick, pig!
Fucking harassment.

388
00:27:33,687 --> 00:27:35,322
You're just gonna leave
him there?

389
00:27:35,356 --> 00:27:38,125
Yeah, he must've done
something to piss Bull off.

390
00:27:39,793 --> 00:27:41,530
We have our laws
and punishments,

391
00:27:41,563 --> 00:27:43,097
streets have theirs.

392
00:27:51,338 --> 00:27:52,806
Where's my boy?

393
00:27:52,840 --> 00:27:54,842
Coach has been keeping 'em late
at practice all week,

394
00:27:54,875 --> 00:27:56,545
getting ready
for the big tournament.

395
00:27:56,578 --> 00:27:58,479
-Oh, yeah? What sport?
-Basketball.

396
00:27:58,513 --> 00:27:59,648
Oh.

397
00:27:59,680 --> 00:28:01,715
He's pretty good too.

398
00:28:01,749 --> 00:28:04,084
He swears he's got
that Mamba mentality.

399
00:28:04,118 --> 00:28:06,253
If he learns to control
that temper of his.

400
00:28:07,421 --> 00:28:10,525
Oh, and how long did it take
you to control yours?

401
00:28:10,559 --> 00:28:12,793
(TEDDY CHUCKLES)

402
00:28:12,826 --> 00:28:15,162
Teddy was a hothead
in his heydays.

403
00:28:15,196 --> 00:28:17,298
I'm still in my heydays.

404
00:28:17,331 --> 00:28:18,633
-He isn't.
-Ouch.

405
00:28:18,667 --> 00:28:21,402
(SANDRA GIGGLES)

406
00:28:21,435 --> 00:28:23,505
Sandra,
you should've seen him.

407
00:28:23,538 --> 00:28:24,872
If a boy did
a double take of me

408
00:28:24,905 --> 00:28:27,741
when I walked by,

409
00:28:27,775 --> 00:28:31,245
Teddy would lose
his ever-lovin' mind.

410
00:28:31,278 --> 00:28:34,616
I used to call him Teddy Bear.
I was 15.

411
00:28:34,649 --> 00:28:38,118
But my parents
called him Grizzly Bear.

412
00:28:38,152 --> 00:28:40,020
They liked him.

413
00:28:40,054 --> 00:28:43,023
Liked that I had
a young warrior protecting me.

414
00:28:43,057 --> 00:28:44,559
They were pretty shocked
to find out

415
00:28:44,593 --> 00:28:46,360
he was half Filipino.

416
00:28:46,393 --> 00:28:47,828
(CHUCKLES)

417
00:28:47,861 --> 00:28:49,330
So you guys got one boy?

418
00:28:49,363 --> 00:28:52,534
Mm, one boy, four girls.

419
00:28:52,567 --> 00:28:53,635
Oh, wow!

420
00:28:53,668 --> 00:28:54,969
(DYANI CHUCKLES)

421
00:28:55,002 --> 00:28:56,804
Yeah, the girls
are all grown up,

422
00:28:56,837 --> 00:28:58,739
scattered all over the place.

423
00:28:58,772 --> 00:29:00,508
Jeffrey was our happy accident.

424
00:29:00,542 --> 00:29:01,842
TEDDY:
All right.

425
00:29:01,875 --> 00:29:03,177
Don't be thinking every shift
we're gonna have time

426
00:29:03,210 --> 00:29:05,412
to sit down and eat,
let alone at home.

427
00:29:05,446 --> 00:29:06,880
You just lucked out.

428
00:29:07,881 --> 00:29:09,750
Not much going on today?

429
00:29:09,783 --> 00:29:11,452
No, it's been pretty quiet.

430
00:29:11,485 --> 00:29:13,320
(EXHALES)

431
00:29:15,923 --> 00:29:18,192
Think I may have
just jinxed us.

432
00:29:19,694 --> 00:29:21,395
DYANI:
Can I ask you a question?

433
00:29:22,564 --> 00:29:23,998
Sure.

434
00:29:24,031 --> 00:29:28,269
Well, I look at you
and I don't see cop.

435
00:29:28,302 --> 00:29:33,240
I mean, I know you were one,
are one, but now Tribal?

436
00:29:33,274 --> 00:29:35,242
How does that happen?

437
00:29:35,276 --> 00:29:36,410
Wasn't my first choice.

438
00:29:36,443 --> 00:29:37,778
TEDDY:
No shit.

439
00:29:41,148 --> 00:29:44,318
Well, I come
from a family of cops.

440
00:29:44,351 --> 00:29:47,354
You know, they were the ones
with like the cop-themed cakes

441
00:29:47,388 --> 00:29:49,290
at the birthday parties,

442
00:29:49,323 --> 00:29:51,492
lots of testosterone
flying around.

443
00:29:52,694 --> 00:29:55,530
You know, my dad had just
been promoted to deputy chief

444
00:29:55,563 --> 00:29:57,732
when I put in
for the department.

445
00:29:57,766 --> 00:29:59,233
He didn't like the idea of me
rolling around

446
00:29:59,266 --> 00:30:01,435
the gutter with the bad guys,
so I told him

447
00:30:01,468 --> 00:30:04,606
it's either his department
where he can keep an eye on me,

448
00:30:04,639 --> 00:30:06,173
or somewhere else.

449
00:30:06,206 --> 00:30:09,143
All right. But why here?
Why Tribal?

450
00:30:10,878 --> 00:30:12,246
I guess his, uh,
shadow was harder

451
00:30:12,279 --> 00:30:15,015
to come out from under
than I thought it would be.

452
00:30:15,049 --> 00:30:17,519
And I also just kinda wanted
to be somewhere far

453
00:30:17,552 --> 00:30:19,086
and, uh, different.

454
00:30:20,321 --> 00:30:21,922
I mean, there's more to it
than that,

455
00:30:21,955 --> 00:30:24,358
but that's the gist of it.

456
00:30:24,391 --> 00:30:27,928
DYANI:
Well, I think your father
should be proud.

457
00:30:28,495 --> 00:30:29,897
Right, Ted?

458
00:30:31,365 --> 00:30:34,134
He likes you. I can tell.
Trust me.

459
00:30:34,168 --> 00:30:38,038
Otherwise, you would be sitting
in the car while he ate.

460
00:30:38,072 --> 00:30:40,742
I'm serious.
I have seen him do it before.

461
00:30:40,775 --> 00:30:42,376
What was...

462
00:30:42,409 --> 00:30:44,411
What was that guy's name,
the deputy?

463
00:30:44,445 --> 00:30:45,780
Dumphrey.

464
00:30:45,814 --> 00:30:47,414
DYANI:
Dumphrey.

465
00:30:47,448 --> 00:30:51,251
So Ted here has the boy
sit in the cop car

466
00:30:51,285 --> 00:30:53,521
while he ate
and napped on the couch.

467
00:30:53,555 --> 00:30:55,623
(CHUCKLING)

468
00:30:55,657 --> 00:30:58,092
DISPATCHER (ON RADIO):
<i>Incoming Priority One.</i>
<i>All units attend.</i>

469
00:30:59,860 --> 00:31:01,895
Sorry, sorry.

470
00:31:03,565 --> 00:31:05,432
I'll pack these up.

471
00:31:10,471 --> 00:31:13,073
TEDDY:
You're looking for Northeast
14th. Tell me where to turn.

472
00:31:13,107 --> 00:31:15,710
-Which road are we on right now?
-TEDDY: 4th parallel south.

473
00:31:15,744 --> 00:31:18,112
DISPATCHER (ON RADIO):
<i>Patching you over to Sheriff's</i>
<i>Department to get you back up.</i>

474
00:31:18,145 --> 00:31:19,913
I swear to God,
if they beat us to our call,

475
00:31:19,947 --> 00:31:21,181
you are walking back
to the station.

476
00:31:21,215 --> 00:31:23,250
How many have we passed so far?
How many roads?

477
00:31:23,283 --> 00:31:24,753
Uh, three.

478
00:31:24,786 --> 00:31:26,554
Oh, shit! Turn!

479
00:31:31,659 --> 00:31:34,061
DISPATCHER (ON RADIO):
<i>Caller has identified suspect</i>
<i>as Elan Graves.</i>

480
00:31:34,094 --> 00:31:35,563
<i>Says he had</i>
<i>to leave the scene</i>

481
00:31:35,597 --> 00:31:38,098
<i>since the suspect's firing off</i>
<i>shots at random.</i>

482
00:31:38,132 --> 00:31:41,335
<i>Female is out front,</i>
<i>in need of medical assistance.</i>

483
00:31:41,368 --> 00:31:42,369
TEDDY:
Shit.

484
00:31:42,403 --> 00:31:45,305
This is gonna be bad.
Elan is highly unstable.

485
00:32:16,805 --> 00:32:19,239
Jesus.
He beat her half to death.

486
00:32:24,378 --> 00:32:25,446
Faint.

487
00:32:25,479 --> 00:32:28,248
You administer CPR.
I'm gonna go clear the house.

488
00:32:29,283 --> 00:32:30,752
Make sure you know
what you're looking at.

489
00:32:30,785 --> 00:32:32,186
They got two boys.

490
00:32:33,086 --> 00:32:35,557
SANDRA:
Bravo 5-5, Code 9, 901 Nora.

491
00:32:35,590 --> 00:32:36,891
Scene not secure.

492
00:32:36,925 --> 00:32:38,893
Have fire stage south
of our cruiser lights.

493
00:32:38,927 --> 00:32:40,762
Making entry, 10-33.

494
00:32:40,795 --> 00:32:45,999
(♪♪♪)

495
00:32:51,405 --> 00:32:52,607
Tribal Police!

496
00:32:52,640 --> 00:32:55,075
Elan, if you're in here,
make yourself known!

